00:20:24.112 --> 00:20:25.894
out of fuckin business.

00:20:26.573 --> 00:20:28.314
I mean that would be no hesitation.

00:20:28.314 --> 00:20:29.545
When it comes to war,

00:20:29.545 --> 00:20:30.660
look, I wish A.J. was here.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.728
I think he's in Oklahoma or

00:20:31.728 --> 00:20:33.446
in Tennessee on business.

00:20:35.366 --> 00:20:39.158
Yeah, I mean, under the context
of the Jets and football

00:20:39.158 --> 00:20:43.848
and business, I will slash
anyone's face with a hose.

00:20:43.848 --> 00:20:44.800
I don't know what that means,

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.191
but if Lizzie is like, if I
came home and Lizzie's like

00:20:47.191 --> 00:20:49.212
I'm starting Lizzie Media,
and we're gonna crush it.

00:20:49.212 --> 00:20:50.558
I'm like that's great.

00:20:50.558 --> 00:20:52.155
I'm gonna put you
directly out of business.

00:20:52.509 --> 00:20:53.803
That would be the answer.

00:20:55.481 --> 00:20:57.710
- [Voiceover] Mike asks,
"Gary, why do you put so much

00:20:57.710 --> 00:21:00.537
emphasis onto sports such as the Jets?"

00:21:01.657 --> 00:21:02.562
- I don't know Mike.

00:21:02.562 --> 00:21:03.538
Truth is I really don't know.

00:21:03.538 --> 00:21:05.813
When I psycho-analyze myself I think

00:21:05.813 --> 00:21:09.296
the Jets specifically was
when I was five, six years old

00:21:09.296 --> 00:21:11.386
was the first Americana thing.

00:21:11.386 --> 00:21:13.313
I often like saying I
learned how to speak English

00:21:13.313 --> 00:21:14.822
while watching the Jets.

00:21:14.822 --> 00:21:16.517
I mean at some level it
was really Scooby Doo,

00:21:16.517 --> 00:21:19.559
and the Great Space
Coaster and Price is Right,

00:21:19.559 --> 00:21:21.463
but the Jets were really
kind of that first

00:21:21.463 --> 00:21:23.947
American thing that I
associated with the kids

00:21:23.947 --> 00:21:25.247
in the neighborhood around.

00:21:25.247 --> 00:21:27.082
You get into rhythm.

00:21:27.082 --> 00:21:28.753
It's like working out or reading.

00:21:28.753 --> 00:21:31.517
My cadence became like I watch the Jets,

00:21:31.517 --> 00:21:34.094
and then you go through all
those emotions over 35 years.

00:21:34.094 --> 00:21:37.089
You start really building a loyalty to it.

00:21:37.089 --> 00:21:40.642
The downs and the downs and the slight ups

00:21:40.642 --> 00:21:42.731
and the downs, and so you know, I think

00:21:42.731 --> 00:21:44.751
I don't know why I put so much emphasis

00:21:44.751 --> 00:21:46.098
around it.

00:21:46.098 --> 00:21:47.282
I don't really have the full pledge thing,

00:21:47.282 --> 00:21:48.670
but that's my best guess.

00:21:49.581 --> 00:21:50.649
- [Voiceover] Ivan asks,

00:21:50.649 --> 00:21:53.203
"I am starting a wedding
invitation and stationary boutique

00:21:53.203 --> 00:21:54.550
called Spokenforco.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:57.266
I publish a post on the
company blog every Tuesday.

00:21:57.266 --> 00:21:59.890
I spend 10 to 15 hours on each post.

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:02.978
I create visuals to promote
these posts on social media.

00:22:02.978 --> 00:22:04.789
However, I realize that I
am getting way more likes

00:22:04.789 --> 00:22:06.368
on my hand drawn lettering
posts compared to these

00:22:06.368 --> 00:22:08.336
non hand drawn ones.

00:22:08.342 --> 00:22:09.451
What should I do?"

00:22:10.617 --> 00:22:13.984
- Vivian, you're spending
way too much time on it

00:22:13.984 --> 00:22:14.727
in my opinion.

00:22:14.727 --> 00:22:16.770
10 to 15 hours feels
completely disproportional

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:18.233
to the value exchange that
you're getting in return.

00:22:18.233 --> 00:22:20.601
You need to figure out
how to do it faster.

00:22:20.601 --> 00:22:22.831
You also need to become
a little less romantic,

00:22:22.831 --> 00:22:24.084
and you need to figure out what your

00:22:24.084 --> 00:22:25.849
micro-version of that is, because content

00:22:25.849 --> 00:22:28.171
is a gateway drug to opportunity,

00:22:28.171 --> 00:22:30.679
and I think your supply
and demand or your value

00:22:30.679 --> 00:22:33.581
and return for the time is off kilter.

00:22:33.581 --> 00:22:36.181
You're also in a space and
you're a part of this world,

00:22:36.181 --> 00:22:38.039
because you love the
design and the creation

00:22:38.039 --> 00:22:39.873
and you're an artist at heart,

00:22:39.873 --> 00:22:41.847
and so I don't wanna tell you what to do,

00:22:41.847 --> 00:22:43.008
but from a business context,

00:22:43.008 --> 00:22:44.726
and that's why you asked it on this show

00:22:44.726 --> 00:22:46.514
I think there's an inefficiency there,

00:22:46.514 --> 00:22:47.884
and you need to figure out how to make

00:22:47.884 --> 00:22:50.299
that 10 to 15 hours
closer to one to two max,

00:22:50.299 --> 00:22:53.178
45 minutes preferably, so you
can do a hell of a lot more.

00:22:53.178 --> 00:22:54.617
Every Tuesday is not enough.

00:22:54.617 --> 00:22:55.987
I need more often.

00:22:55.987 --> 00:22:57.891
The only way I can get
it more often from you

00:22:57.891 --> 00:23:00.608
is if you allow yourself to go faster.

00:23:00.608 --> 00:23:02.767
This goes back to an earlier
question in this marathon

00:23:02.767 --> 00:23:04.091
of Ts and Is.

00:23:04.091 --> 00:23:07.132
I think you're going way too
down the perfection variable.

00:23:07.132 --> 00:23:09.733
To prove out my point,
I would ask you to try

00:23:09.733 --> 00:23:11.242
to do what you can do.

00:23:11.242 --> 00:23:11.985
Do me a favor.

00:23:11.985 --> 00:23:13.750
Next Tuesday, spend two hours on it.

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:16.048
See what it does, and
see what the results are.

00:23:16.048 --> 00:23:17.140
You may learn from that,

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:18.812
and if you hate what happens,

00:23:18.812 --> 00:23:20.089
and there's not a lot of engagement

00:23:20.089 --> 00:23:22.294
do it one more time, and
if you can get me to three

00:23:22.294 --> 00:23:24.245
strikes where it doesn't work
in three straight Tuesdays

00:23:24.245 --> 00:23:25.684
then you can go back to doing your thing,

00:23:25.684 --> 00:23:28.442
but my gut tells me
that won't be the case.

